{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git show --stat --oneline 80cbebc && git show 80cbebc:conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md | tail -35'","aggregated_output":"80cbebc T-103: rejections carry a reason (#7)\n conformance/app/server.js                   |  11 +-\n conformance/app/tests/reject-reason.test.js | 254 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md | 151 +++++++++++++++++\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md        |  70 +++++++-\n 4 files changed, 474 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)\n\n- `tests/health.test.js` (4 `assert.deepStrictEqual` calls on `GET /health` bodies) and `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (3 exact `JSON.stringify` matches on `GET /health` bodies) — both assert only the aggregate `{ ok, queue, approvals: {pending,sent,rejected,blocked_recipient} }` shape from the `/health` summary endpoint. This ticket does not touch `/health` or its counts; the per-approval `reason` field lives on `/api/state` records, which `/health` never returns verbatim. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- `tests/conformance.test.js` test `\"6b. reject: closes the proposal, nothing sends\"` asserts `r.status === \"rejected\"` (a single-property `assert.strictEqual`, not a full-object/deepStrictEqual match) plus outbox length and the post-reject `approve` 409. Adding a `reason` key to the reject response body and to the approval record does not change `.status` and is not caught by a property-level assertion. **Not affected, no edits needed.**\n- No test file anywhere does `assert.deepStrictEqual` (or an exact `JSON.stringify`/full-body match) against an individual approval object from `/api/state` or against the full `POST /reject` response body.\n\n**Conclusion: zero existing tests require amendment.** This is an audited result, not an assumption — the test-author does not need to touch any pre-existing test file for this ticket; `tests/reject-reason.test.js` is a purely additive new file.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- App lives in `conformance/app/` (zero-dependency Node 18+; see `conformance/SPEC.md`).\n- Tests go in `conformance/app/tests/` — new file `tests/reject-reason.test.js`, same style as the existing suites (node:test, spawn the real server on its own port with a temp DATA_DIR).\n- Run tests from `conformance/app/` with `node --test tests/reject-reason.test.js`.\n\n## Labels\n\nNo `external` label — rejecting a proposal cannot trigger a send (outbox is untouched by this ticket); this only adds metadata to the approval record.\n\n## Log\n\n- 2026-07-12: ticket created by the operator; State → Ready. First ticket of the loop trial (dispatcher runs stage-to-stage without per-stage operator go).\n- 2026-07-12: planner froze the `POST /api/approvals/:id/reject` reason contract and the `reason` field on rejected `/api/state` approvals; audited all three existing test files and found zero exact-body collisions (see \"Existing test audit\") — `tests/reject-reason.test.js` is purely additive, no pre-existing test needs amendment; branch `ticket/T-103-reject-reason` created off `main`; State → In progress.\n- 2026-07-12: planner (Claude Code) completed the frozen contract and branch/worktree setup; ledger cost $1.0881249. State → Blocked-Escalated because the wrapper reported: \"WARNING: installed Claude Code (2.1.201 (Claude Code)) != pinned (2.1.207). Run adapters/contract-test.sh before continuing.\" Javier must run that contract test or reconcile the installed/pinned version, then explicitly authorize resumption.\n- 2026-07-12: operator resolved the adapter escalation: `scripts/adapters/contract-test.sh` passed against Claude Code 2.1.201 and Codex 0.144.1, and `CLAUDE_CODE_PINNED=2.1.201` is now set in `~/.factory/global.env`; State → In progress and stage-to-stage supervision resumed.\n- 2026-07-12: test author added `tests/reject-reason.test.js` with one acceptance test each for: exact reason storage and response; null resolution for missing/non-string reasons; immutable rejection with exact `409`; and reason persistence across `SIGKILL` + restart. All four criteria were expressible as tests; no demo-check-only items.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) committed four acceptance tests at `672a598`; new suite fails 4/4 for the expected missing behavior while all 15 existing tests pass; no implementation code changed; ledger cost $0.4749.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author verification expanded criterion 3 to cover every reachable non-pending status (`rejected`, `sent`, and `blocked_recipient`), asserting the exact `409` body and byte-for-byte unchanged approval record; the four acceptance tests still fail 4/4 for missing contract behavior, while all 15 existing tests pass. All criteria remain test-expressible; no demo-check items.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) completed sequencer-selected verification at `f371048`; coverage now includes all reachable non-pending statuses, acceptance tests fail 4/4 as intended, and existing tests pass 15/15; ledger cost $0.4943.\n- 2026-07-12: State → Blocked-Escalated before the builder started because the wrapper refused exactly: \"daily cap would be exceeded (spent $8.9678 + reserve $1.50 > $10.00) — refusing. See runbooks/operator.md.\" Javier must resolve or reset the daily budget through the operator runbook and explicitly authorize resumption; no builder run or cost was recorded.\n- 2026-07-12: operator confirmed the daily-cap refusal was correct and raised `DAILY_CAP_USD` to $13.00 on main while retaining the machine-level $15.00 cap; State → In progress and stage-to-stage supervision resumed.\n- 2026-07-12: builder (Claude Code) implemented the frozen reject-reason contract in `conformance/app/server.js` without touching tests; all 19 tests pass (15 existing + 4 acceptance), commit `f3d85bb`; ledger cost $0.5681364000000001.\n- 2026-07-12 22:36:03: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The frozen unknown-ID contract is untested. The builder changed reject-response serialization to remove the internal `code` field, but tests only verify exact `409` bodies. An implementation that fixes `409` while returning the wrong `404` body would pass all 19 tests. Add a test asserting an unknown approval returns HTTP `404` with exactly `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such approval\" }`. Criteria 1–4 are otherwise adequately tested. Commit order and test immutability are correct, and the full suite independently passes 19/19. Cost $0.2206.\n- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) addressed reviewer round 1 by adding exact unknown-approval HTTP 404/body coverage at `257619e`; targeted suite passes 5/5 and full suite passes 20/20; only `tests/reject-reason.test.js` changed; ledger cost $0.2461.\n- 2026-07-12 22:40:20: reviewer round 2: APPROVE — The added test correctly asserts both HTTP `404` and the exact frozen body `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such approval\" }`; it would catch the prior leaked `code` field. Criteria 1–4 remain adequately tested. The implementation matches the frozen contract without scope creep, original acceptance tests were unchanged by the builder, the requested regression test is an additive later commit, commit order is correct, and the independently rerun full suite passes 20/20. Cost $0.1490.\n- 2026-07-12: narrator (Claude Code) committed `conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md` at `60a3ef7` with fresh 20/20 tests and live local evidence; ledger cost $0.6907641999999999. State → Review, awaiting operator. Main-ledger total is $3.4570255; including the earlier real test-author run recorded only in the worktree ledger ($0.4749), full actual role-run cost is $3.9319255.\n- 2026-07-12: PR #7 opened for operator review: https://github.com/nysa-company/software-factory/pull/7. CI status could not be read with the factory `GH_TOKEN`; GitHub returned `Resource not accessible by personal access token` for GraphQL checks and REST Actions/status/check-runs. Javier must inspect PR #7 checks, then approve + merge or 